WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:10.850
"Quena Raymi" is a very special festival held
once a year in the Peruvian Andes.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:16.290
It's a tree-planting ceremony -- attended
by over 200 men, women and children from various

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:23.850
villages in the area.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.869
Once the festivities are over, they begin
their hike up the mountain -- carrying shovels

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:34.120
and other tools, and provisions with them
... ((00:36)) PLUS infants and the saplings

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:39.800
-- even the llamas come along.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.130
Their two-hour trek takes them to an altitude
of over four thousand meters above sea-level.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:51.160
They follow anicent paths once used by their
ancestors.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.999
The Incas lived in harmony with their environment.

00:00:53.999 --> 00:00:59.579
For today's population, the idea is to give
back what they have taken from nature.

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:07.360
The past few centuries have seen the area
almost completely deforested, with no effort

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.409
to replenish the devastated woodlands.

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:16.070
These people are the first generation to recognize
that something has to change.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:23.540
Hermogenes, one of the village leaders, is
here with his family.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:27.500
"It's hard to dig holes in the ground here.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.049
You might dislodge rocks -- you can never
rule out accidents.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.369
You have to be extremely careful.

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:49.100
"There are no trees left here -- and no firewood
to gather.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.590
So I'm glad that we're planting new trees.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:59.799
My friends and neighbors have all come along
to help.

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:03.890
Constantino Aucca is the man behind the project.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:10.100
He set up an NGO called the "Association for
Andean Ecosystems" -- or ECOAN -- in 2001.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.060
He and his team want to plant 25 thousand
saplings today.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.290
They have to work quickly so that the roots
won't dry out.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:24.830
"If there's no vegetation or trees, the water
will flow straight from the mountain down

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:32.570
into the valley, and cause landslides, before
it continues on to the sea.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:38.060
The new trees we're planting will absorb the
moisture that nature gives to us -- mist and

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.220
rain.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:50.250
The trees are the ONLY way we have of storing
the water."

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.670
The tropical glaciers are the most important
source of water in the Andes.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:03:01.250
But global warming is causing them to melt
away at a growing pace.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:06.570
Entire swathes of mountain terrain used to
be covered with polylepis trees -- a species

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.590
only found in South America.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:13.790
It's highly resilient, and can withstand extreme
weather conditions.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:21.130
At night, temperatures here can drop to minus
20 degrees Celsius -- in both the winter and

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.280
summer.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:26.630
The trees at these high altitudes therefore
grow very slowly.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:31.290
Over the last 19 years, the biologists from
the NGO have been observing changes in the

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.480
local climate.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:42.200
"People who come here expect to see huge forests
with tall trees blocking out the sun.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.700
What they don't appreciate is that we're 4,400
meters above sea level.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:52.150
In some places, the tree line is as low as
3,500 meters.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:58.410
But here it's different."

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:02.350
More woodland means more liquid in the overall
water cycle.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:07.880
The hope is that eventually this would enable
the glaciers to reverse their retreat.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:15.730
"When there is precipitation, when it rains,
the trees ensure that the water does not simply

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.739
disappear.

00:04:16.739 --> 00:04:22.889
Instead, it is stored by the trees' roots
and by the moss that grows everywhere.

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:27.750
Otherwise it would evaporate far more quickly
especially when the sun's shining, and be

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:36.490
carried away by the wind."

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.599
The slower the water makes its way down from
the mountains, the longer it remains available

00:04:40.599 --> 00:04:43.639
in the villages in the valley -- all year
round.

00:04:43.639 --> 00:04:48.770
Normally this would be the wet season, but
rainfall has decreased -- something the villagers

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:53.800
are all too aware of.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.389
The reforestation project includes the tree
nurseries managed by local people.

00:04:58.389 --> 00:05:04.270
In Hermogenes' village, the saplings are nurtured
for 12 months, until they're sturdy enough

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.240
to be planted.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.930
Their survival rate has now reached almost
90 percent.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.870
ECOAN pays the villagers money for the trees.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:18.330
The association itself is funded by private
donations.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.400
Some of the tree nursuries are now getting
their own greenhouses, in order to provide

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.819
better protection for the plants.

00:05:24.819 --> 00:05:28.370
And that also means new job opportunities.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:34.870
This kind of work is hard to get, so it's
a sound opportunity for us.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:39.460
Not just for me as a technical specialist
but also for my younger colleagues.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:46.050
Logistically they need a lot of people.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:50.479
And that also applies to the tree-planting
enterprise, which involves villagers from

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:53.190
many local communities.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:58.080
They're committed to the project -- even if
its fruits will only be enjoyed by the generations

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:58.639
to come.

